title: A server name containing __ lets /all bypass the profile
updated: 2026-11-06T04:16:44Z
---

Found by mcp-hub-worker during k68 (2026-11-06). /all reads everything before the first __ of a prefixed name as the server. With entries p and p__x and a profile allowing [p], /all tools/call p__x__echo succeeds (and since k68 p__x's prompts leak the same way, the prompt filter uses the same split). A profile allowing [p__x] sees none of its own tools. Separately, two entries can produce the same /all name (p + tool x__echo vs p__x + tool echo); the first wins.
Chosen by the orchestrating agent (not the maintainer) while the maintainer was away: Option B -- Aggregate remembers which server each wrapped tool/prompt came from, and the filters decide by that origin, not by splitting the name. No config change.
Left open for the maintainer: Option A -- refuse __ in server names in Config (with the JSON path), which would also remove the name collisions but narrows the config surface. The collisions stay a known gap until then.
Done: profile filtering on /all by origin for tools and prompts (list and call/get); regression tests with p and p__x for both directions; the collision behaviour pinned by a test (first wins, documented).

